  "_meta": {
    "title": "Expand / zoom out video (LTX-2.5 + IC-LoRA Outpaint)",
    "description": "Core ComfyUI nodes only. Video outpainting with the distilled LTX-2.5 22B model and oumoumad's LTX-2.3 22B IC-LoRA Outpaint (LTX-2 Community License), wired like vfx_clean_plate: LoraLoaderModelOnly -> GetICLoRAParameters -> LTXVAddGuide(guide clip, frame_idx 0, strength 1) on an empty latent of the canvas size, 8 ManualSigmas, euler_ancestral, LTXVDualCFGGuider cfg 1, LTXVCropGuides before decode. Guide = the source frames scaled into the centre (or one side) of a PURE BLACK canvas (EmptyImage color 0 + ImageCompositeMasked): black is the LoRA's 'generate here' sentinel (grey does not work). Frames: the first 121 at native fps (VideoTemporalCrop), trimmed to the largest 8n+1 (ComfyMathExpression + ImageFromBatch; no resampling, speed unchanged); a second VideoTemporalCrop of that length carries the matching audio. Canvas long edge 1024 (builder option 1280), multiples of 32. Conditioning and audio-latent frame rate = the source fps. After decode the generation is upscaled to the expanded output size and the ORIGINAL frames are composited back over their rect with a wide FeatherMask ramp (48 px, padded sides only). Source fps and audio go to CreateVideo. The builder (src/lib/oj/videoExpand.ts) sets canvas, rect, feather and the size expressions; everything that depends on the real decoded frame size is computed in-graph from GetImageSize (ComfyMathExpression): node 23 fits the source (even size, expanded frame <= 2560 px; identity for normal clips), nodes 42/43 give the output size and 44/45 the paste-back offsets, so a run with a wrong recorded width/height still pastes back in place. Dark footage: the model card suggests a gamma 2.0 / 0.5 round trip; no core node does gamma, so it is not offered."
  }
